WHAT SHIPPED (full parity — no scope narrowing)
  The Fleet Telemetry signal-subscription configurator, an Apple-HIG sheet (NavigationStack + scrolling
  body + pinned footer). Every web region + behaviour reproduced:
    • The 10 INTERVAL_OPTIONS (0==500ms … 86400==24h) with label + descriptive tier + accent tint,
      and the `… || INTERVAL_OPTIONS[3]` 10s fallback.
    • All 8 PRESETS (⚡ Real-time Driving / ⚖️ Balanced / 🔋 Low Power / 🏎️ Track Mode / 💰 Cost Saver /
      😴 Sleep Watch / 🔧 Diagnostics / 🗺️ Trip Logger) — each transcribed 1:1 as pure category→selection
      + category→interval rules (every "everything else" arm included).
    • The CATEGORY_ICONS lucide map → SF Symbols with the `|| Zap` → bolt.fill fallback.
    • Master controls: preset chips, Select-All/Deselect-All toggle, master cadence menu (applies to all),
      and the case-insensitive search field.
    • Per-category collapsible section: disclosure chevron, tri-state checkbox (all/partial/none),
      glyph, name, (sel/total) count, and "Set all…" cadence menu.
    • Per-signal row: checkbox, monospaced name, cadence menu; deselected rows dim (web opacity-40).
    • Footer: "{n} signals selected • {x} at 500ms • {y} at 10s" roll-up + Cancel + the count-stamped
      "Subscribe {n} Signals" (disabled at 0).
  States: the web component is presentational + prop-driven with NO fetch, so it has no loading / error /
  stale / offline branch — and neither does this parity (fabricating an unreachable network state would
  be scope INVENTION, not parity). The branches that exist are reproduced in full: `.data` (grouped list)
  and the two empties `.emptyNoSignals` / `.emptyNoMatch`, each a friendly message, never a blank box.
  Architecture: pure Adapter+Projection (domain + reducers), an @Observable @MainActor SignalConfigModel
  (P1/S8) bound by the view, the P1/S10 string facade (table "SignalConfigModal", English fallbacks, no
  English literals in code), and a P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry seam emitting slug "SignalConfigModal"
  once on presentation. Full VoiceOver labels/values/traits, Dynamic Type (Font.TS), Reduce-Motion (TSFadeIn).

